## 2. 📘 AGENTS.md — "The README for AI Agents"

Think of `AGENTS.md` as the **project onboarding doc specifically for AI agents**. While `README.md` is for humans, `AGENTS.md` is for machines.

### Key Properties

| Property | Detail |
|---|---|
| **Created by** | Agentic AI Foundation (Factory.ai + others) |
| **Format** | Plain Markdown, `##` headers + bullet points |
| **Location** | Root of repo (or any subdirectory for monorepos) |
| **Supported by** | Cursor, Codex, Copilot, Gemini CLI, Jules, Devin, Aider, Windsurf |
| **Adopted by** | 60,000+ projects as of Feb 2026 |

### Structure

```markdown
## Project Overview
This is a FastAPI microservice for user authentication.

## Build & Run
- `pip install -r requirements.txt`
- `uvicorn main:app --reload`
- `pytest tests/ -v`

## Architecture
- `/app/routes/` — API endpoints
- `/app/models/` — SQLAlchemy models  
- `/app/services/` — Business logic

## Conventions
- Use Pydantic v2 for all request/response models
- All endpoints must have OpenAPI docstrings
- Error responses follow RFC 7807

## Boundaries
- NEVER modify `/migrations/` directly — use Alembic
- NEVER expose internal IDs — use UUIDs
```

### Hierarchy (for Monorepos)

```
repo/
├── AGENTS.md              ← Global: applies everywhere
├── frontend/
│   └── AGENTS.md          ← Overrides for frontend
├── backend/
│   ├── AGENTS.md          ← Overrides for backend
│   └── auth-service/
│       └── AGENTS.md      ← Most specific: auth service
```

> [!IMPORTANT]
> **2026 research finding**: Monolithic `AGENTS.md` files can increase inference costs by up to **159%**. Use **tiered injection** — break into smaller, scoped files so only task-relevant instructions are loaded.

