## 3. 🛠️ SKILL.md — "Teachable Skills / Capabilities"

Skills are **modular, reusable instruction packages** that give an AI agent a specialized capability on demand.

### Key Properties

| Property | Detail |
|---|---|
| **Created by** | Anthropic (Oct 2025), open standard (Dec 2025) |
| **Format** | YAML frontmatter + Markdown body |
| **Supported by** | OpenAI Codex, GitHub Copilot, VS Code, Cursor |
| **Key principle** | **Progressive disclosure** — load only when needed |

### Directory Structure

```
.skills/
├── deploy-to-aws/
│   ├── SKILL.md           ← Required: instructions
│   ├── scripts/
│   │   └── deploy.sh      ← Helper scripts
│   └── references/
│       └── aws-guide.md   ← Reference docs
│
├── database-migration/
│   ├── SKILL.md
│   └── scripts/
│       └── migrate.py
```

### SKILL.md Format

```yaml
---
name: deploy-to-aws
description: Deploy the application to AWS ECS using Terraform
license: MIT
compatibility:
  os: [linux, macos]
  tools: [terraform, aws-cli]
metadata:
  author: platform-team
  version: "1.2.0"
---

# Deploy to AWS

## Prerequisites
- AWS CLI configured with appropriate credentials
- Terraform >= 1.5.0 installed

## Steps
1. Run `terraform init` in `/infra/aws/`
2. Run `terraform plan -var-file=env/prod.tfvars`
3. Review the plan output
4. Run `terraform apply` only after human approval

## Common Issues
- If "insufficient permissions", check IAM role has ECS:* policies
- If state lock error, run `terraform force-unlock <LOCK_ID>`
```

### How Progressive Disclosure Works

```
Agent sees task "deploy to production"
           │
           ▼
    ┌─────────────────────────┐
    │ 1. Scan SKILL.md names  │ ← Only loads name + description (cheap)
    │    & descriptions       │
    └──────────┬──────────────┘
               │ Match: "deploy-to-aws"
               ▼
    ┌─────────────────────────┐
    │ 2. Load SKILL.md body   │ ← Full instructions loaded (moderate)
    └──────────┬──────────────┘
               │ Needs deploy.sh
               ▼
    ┌─────────────────────────┐
    │ 3. Load scripts/        │ ← Resources loaded on demand (targeted)
    └─────────────────────────┘
```

> [!NOTE]
> **Skills vs Rules**: Rules define *character* ("always use TypeScript"). Skills define *competence* ("here's how to deploy to AWS"). An agent can have many skills but loads them only when relevant.

