## 5. 🔌 MCP (Model Context Protocol) — "USB-C for AI Agents"

MCP is the **universal standard for connecting AI agents to external tools and data**. Created by Anthropic (Nov 2024), now adopted by OpenAI, Google, Microsoft, and LangChain.

### Architecture

```mermaid
graph LR
    A[AI Agent / Host] --> B[MCP Client]
    B -->|JSON-RPC 2.0| C[MCP Server: GitHub]
    B -->|JSON-RPC 2.0| D[MCP Server: Database]
    B -->|JSON-RPC 2.0| E[MCP Server: Slack]
    B -->|JSON-RPC 2.0| F[MCP Server: Custom API]
```

### What MCP Servers Provide

| Capability | Description | Example |
|---|---|---|
| **Tools** | Executable functions the agent can call | `create_pull_request()`, `query_database()` |
| **Resources** | Read-only data sources | File contents, API docs, database schemas |
| **Prompts** | Pre-built prompt templates | "Summarize this PR", "Generate migration" |

### Popular MCP Servers

| Server | What it does |
|---|---|
| GitHub MCP | Create PRs, manage issues, search repos |
| Filesystem MCP | Read/write local files |
| PostgreSQL MCP | Query databases, inspect schemas |
| Slack MCP | Send messages, read channels |
| Browser MCP | Navigate, screenshot, interact with pages |
| Context7 | Fetch live, version-specific docs (see below) |

### Configuration Example (Claude Desktop)

```json
{
  "mcpServers": {
    "github": {
      "command": "npx",
      "args": ["-y", "@modelcontextprotocol/server-github"],
      "env": { "GITHUB_TOKEN": "ghp_xxx" }
    },
    "postgres": {
      "command": "npx",
      "args": ["-y", "@modelcontextprotocol/server-postgres", "postgresql://localhost/mydb"]
    }
  }
}
```

> [!TIP]
> **Mental model**: Rule files tell the agent *who it is*. Skills tell it *what it can learn*. MCP tells it *what it can reach*.

