## 📊 Master Cheat Sheet: What Goes Where

| What you want to control | File / Mechanism | Supported By |
|---|---|---|
| Coding style & conventions | Rule files (`.cursorrules`, `CLAUDE.md`, etc.) | Tool-specific |
| Project context for agents | `AGENTS.md` | Universal (all tools) |
| Specialized capabilities | `SKILL.md` + scripts | Codex, Copilot, Cursor |
| Repeatable procedures | Workflows (`.agents/workflows/`) | Tool-specific |
| External tool access | MCP Servers | Claude, Copilot, Cursor, VS Code |
| Live documentation | Context7 (MCP) | Any MCP-compatible tool |
| Cross-session memory | Memory files (`CLAUDE.md`, `GEMINI.md`) | Tool-specific |
| Task tracking | `task.md`, `implementation_plan.md` | Framework-specific |
| Agent-to-agent comms | A2A, ACP, TAP | Framework-specific |
| Cost optimization | Prompt caching, tiered injection | API-level |

